DE DE FABRICATION</invention-title><citations><patent-citations><patcit ucid="EP-0709906-A1" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>EP</country><doc-number>0709906</doc-number><kind>A1</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-10302828-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>10302828</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y"  name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-2000011993-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>2000011993</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="AE" name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-2000011994-A"  status="new"><document-id status="new"  format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>2000011994</doc-number><kind>A</kind> </document-id><sources><source category="AE" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="WO-1998028804-A1" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>WO</country><doc-number>1998028804</doc-number> <kind>A1</kind> </document-id> <sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1113511A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ISSHIKI NOBUYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KAJIURA YOSHIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KAO CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI ATSUSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ISSHIKI, NOBUYUKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAJIURA, YOSHIO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAO CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI, ATSUSHI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ISSHIKI NOBUYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KAJIURA YOSHIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI ATSUSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ISSHIKI, NOBUYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAJIURA, YOSHIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI, ATSUSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A lithium secondary cell comprising an anode and cathode containing an active material capable of absorbing and releasing lithium ions, wherein the anode is a porous sintered body made of a lithium transition metal oxide, the porosity is 15 to 60%, and the conductivity is more than 0.1 mS/cm.  Since the material is sufficiently sintered so that the conductivity may be more than 0.1 mS/cm, the bonding power of the primary particles of the sintered body is strong, and therefore the primary particles do not come off and the electrodes do not collapse even if the sintered body expands or shrinks because of the charging/discharging.  Since the mechanical strength is great, the anode can have a larger area.  The electrolyte penetrates well into the sintered body because of its 15 to 60% porosity, and consequently the internal resistance is low.  Thus a lithium secondary cell having a high capacity and excellent cycle characteristics is provided.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un accumulateur au lithium comprenant une anode et une cathode contenant un matériau actif capable d'absorber et de dégager des ions lithium, l'anode étant un corps fritté poreux en oxyde de métal de transition lithium, présentant une porosité de 15 à 60 % et une conductivité de plus de 0,1 mS/cm. Etant donné que le matériau est suffisamment fritté pour que la conductivité soit supérieure à 0,1 mS/cm, le pouvoir agglomérant des particules primaires du corps fritté est élevé, les particules ne se détachent pas et les électrodes ne s'affaissent pas même si le corps fritté se dilate ou se rétracte sous l'effet d'une charge/décharge. Du fait que la résistance mécanique est élevée, l'anode peut présenter une superficie supérieure. L'électrolyte pénètre bien dans le corps fritté en raison de la porosité de 15 à 60 %, et la résistance interne est donc faible. Ainsi, un accumulateur au lithium à haute capacité et présentant des caractéristiques de cyclage excellentes est produit.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-docume